{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNBkrXJMmzaM3S3QpkhM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `.ard/302/triage-lead.md` and routed issue #302 as **done**. The `triage:engineer` role plans it and the `engineer` worker builds it.\n\nThe issue asks for a clear code change: `ard serve` checks GitHub connectivity and permissions at startup, accepts a personal access token for live runs, and falls back to the `gh` CLI's token when no credentials are set. It also updates the docs. I checked that the code the issue cites exists: `internal/servecmd/serve.go` refuses `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` outside `--dry-run`, and `internal/github/auth.go` marks token auth \"Development only\".\n\nThe engineer is the only triage role in the repository, so it has to plan everything, including the parts a product-manager, architect or documentation-planner would normally cover. No reviewer has a `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so `eng-review` runs on the pull request anyway and I added no `review:` entries.\n\nThings a maintainer should know, also listed in the file:\n- **Self-review needs a decision.** GitHub won't let a user approve their own pull request, so with a PAT ard can't approve its own work. The issue leaves the fix to triage. Either ard posts a comment review carrying its verdict and the merger trusts ard's own record of it, or the docs require reviews from a second identity. The engineer plan should pick one, but a maintainer may want to confirm it because it changes the merge gate.\n- **The commit-audit workflow under `.github/` should only be documented.** Agents may not change `.github/`, and it is a protected path in the config."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":769,"cache_read_input_tokens":12732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":769},"output_tokens":531,"ser